      "path": "/books/al-kafi:3:4:25:14",
      "text": [
        " رَأَيْتُ أَبَا الْحَسَنِ ( عليه السلام ) وَ قَدْ سَجَدَ بَعْدَ الصَّلَاةِ فَبَسَطَ ذِرَاعَيْهِ عَلَى الْأَرْضِ وَ أَلْصَقَ جُؤْجُؤَهُ بِالْأَرْضِ فِي دُعَائِهِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Ja’far Bin Ali who said, ",
          "‘I saw Abu Al-Hassan<sup>asws</sup> and he<sup>asws</sup> was prostrating after the <span class=\"iTxt\">Salāt</span>. So he<sup>asws</sup> spread out his<sup>asws</sup> arms upon the ground and paste his<sup>asws</sup> chest upon the ground’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "14. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn abu ‘Umayr from Ja‘far ibn Ali who has said the following: “I saw abu al-Hassan, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, doing sajdah for after Salah (prayer), his arms spread on the ground and his chest and belly placed on the ground when praying.” "
        ]
      }
